premise='FixedR/B8 default/nooverride. Full original W24/25/26/27 fixture gates apply, including valid actual compiled registry objects/healthy owned bench, successful reaching move after-effects or initial-entry tail and normal preceding UI/scene/ability/item/form/party/callback dependencies unless a named guard/negative result is considered. W24 excludes earlier user replacement/Pursuit KO/terminal state; W26 has a real statsDropped write after entry reset and no earlier true exit, and replacement-entry completes without another exit/terminal. Primary records are exact fixed inputs, not proof that every runtime binary was compiled from them. No actual game/Ruby/native/serialization execution, all-domain qualification or new future public helper/API mandate.'
manual=[
 ('RC-PRIMARYSPECIES','EEVEE3508–3542','The complete default Eevee record includes BATONPASS at level35 and as a TutorMove; W24 supplies that actual move with PP at level50, rather than assuming constructor default last-four retention.'),
 ('RC-PRIMARYMOVES','BATONPASS5718–5726/ROAR6309–6319','Complete default BATONPASS FunctionCode is SwitchOutUserPassOnEffects; ROAR is SwitchOutTargetStatusMove. Their original fields are preserved, with normal compilation/lookup a stated premise.'),
 ('RC-MOVEFACTORY','from_pokemon_move57–69','A valid Pokemon::Move function code chooses the matching existing Battle::Move constant; absent constant uses Unimplemented. Thus the named default codes route to the fully read classes under normal registry inputs.'),
 ('B17-SWITCH','CanSwitchIn9–34/CanChoose92–97','A legal bench requires party index in bounds, present non-egg same-owner healthy object not already active. CanChooseNonActive returns upon first legal CanSwitchIn; it does not depend on internalBattle.'),
 ('RC-SWITCHMOVES','BatonPass123–145','BatonPass fails before use if no legal bench. Its after-use stage returns for fainted user/zero hits/no bench, invokes Pursuit, then rechecks user fainted before asking for a replacement.'),
 ('RC-SWITCHMOVES','BatonPass132–144','A reached owner-choice replacement calls GetReplacement without random=true; negative return exits before replacement. A nonnegative return recalls/replaces with batonPass=true, clears the slot choice, clears moldBreaker, invokes entry and then marks that battler switched.'),
 ('B17-SWITCH','GetReplacement206–217/SwitchInBetween132–135','Nonrandom GetReplacement invokes SwitchInBetween(checkLaxOnly=true), whose normal player route asks the party screen and whose nonplayer route uses replacement AI. No internalBattle gate wraps this path.'),
 ('R05','RecordedSwitch74–78/PlaybackSwitch182–186','Recording SwitchInBetween appends every normally returned selection, including negative, then returns it. Playback returns the current switch entry and advances only switchindex, without calling live UI or pbRandom.'),
 ('RC-AFTERMOVE','EffectsAfterMove87–174','After-move processing calls target forced switching first, then intermediate item/ability processing, and user after-use effect only if that user was not already switched. This is reached within move execution, before battle-loop end-of-round.'),
 ('B17-SWITCH','Recall220–226/Replace274–285','Replacement calls recall/OnSwitchOut/lineup/messages then initializes the new party entry with the passed baton flag, reorders battle party order, sends out and optionally recalculates priority. Normal effects/callback completion is required; no rollback is supplied here.'),
 ('RC-COMMAND','ClearChoice5–11','ClearChoice changes only the actual slot choice to None/0/nil/−1; it neither edits previously recorded commands nor permanently blocks later command selection.'),
 ('RC-SWITCHMOVES','Roar153–220','Roar failure checks include unsuppressed Suction Cups, Ingrain, applicable wild-level/escape conditions and trainer eligible-bench existence. W25 explicitly passes these gates; it is not a blanket all-target eligibility statement.'),
 ('RC-SWITCHMOVES','Roar202–219','A qualified nonwild target forced switch calls GetReplacement(random=true), never owner-choice SwitchInBetween; after replacement it clears choice, runs entry, marks the target switched and stops after the first successful target.'),
 ('B17-SWITCH','GetReplacement206–217','Random replacement builds actual eligible same-team indices in iterator order, returns−1 if empty, otherwise selects choices[pbRandom(length)]; the recording wrapper records that random result and does not create a switch entry.'),
 ('R04','CanSwitchIn53–56/CanChoose92–97','Arena overrides CanSwitchIn to false for every input; inherited CanChooseNonActive therefore finds no legal bench, so BatonPass fails before asking even if party objects would qualify in Tower.'),
 ('R04','EORSwitch58–72','Arena replacement judges first subject to decision gates, then takes the next sequential party entry for a fainted side if available, using direct Replace and Entry rather than SwitchInBetween or generic random eligibility enumeration.'),
 ('R04','AsActive85–94/ordinaryEntry316–374','Arena defines an AsActive reset method, but ordinary entry invokes Participated instead. Sequential replacement therefore does not itself invoke that Arena count/skill/baseline reset; separate actual command/EOR/initial-start paths retain their own writes.'),
 ('B17-SWITCH','EORSwitch142–204','The optional player switch-style question on opponent replacement still requires internalBattle true and the other source gates. Its absence in facilities does not guard move-after-use or entry-item owner-choice replacement.'),
 ('RC-PRIMARYITEMS','EJECTPACK851–859','The complete default EJECTPACK item record is present with its exact price/pocket/flags/description fields. Effective held-item status and actual stat loss are separate executable guards, not guaranteed by the description.'),
 ('RC-START','Start247–317/Loop322–347','Recording captures its properties before delegating to normal start. Normal core setup/sendout/weather/terrain and OnAllEntering occur before BattleLoop invokes the first command phase; thus an entry-tail selection can be recorded while roundindex remains−1.'),
 ('B17-SWITCH','OnAllEntering303–311/Entry316–374','Entry clears prior drop flags unless skip_event_reset, processes entrant effects/abilities/items in priority order, then checks every priority battler itemOnStatDropped before damage-taken abilities and stops on first true; the final tail clears both flags.'),
 ('RC-ABILITYEFFECTS','INTIMIDATE2851–2868','The complete actual Intimidate handler considers nearby opponents, invokes LowerAttackStatStageIntimidate and dependent intimidated callbacks/item checks. The fixture requires actual successful lowering; merely possessing Intimidate does not establish it.'),
 ('RC-STATSTAGES','Lower123–301/Intimidate303–356','Successful normal lowering reaches LowerStatStageBasic with a positive clamped increment, updates the stage and sets statsLoweredThisRound/statsDropped true. Substitute/immunities/Mist/minimum/Contrary/MirrorArmor can prevent that receiver from this write; the W26 real-loss premise excludes those alternatives.'),
 ('RC-BATTLERITEM','ItemOnStatDropped384–388','ItemOnStatDropped returns false before dispatch without statsDropped or with inactive item; otherwise it dispatches current actual held item, receiver, move_user and battle to OnStatLoss.'),
 ('B17-BATTLER','itemActive421–428','Default itemActive rejects fainted receiver, Embargo, Magic Room, corrosive gas and active Klutz. Item identity itself routes via the actual held-item getter and handler lookup.'),
 ('RC-HANDLERS','HandlerHashSymbol148–197/ItemHash294–295','The symbol handler map canonicalizes id-capable objects, resolves an exact registered handler (then conditional registrations), and trigger calls it with item id plus arguments or yields nil if absent. ItemHandlerHash adds no override.'),
 ('RC-ITEMEFFECTS','trigger53–56/OnStatLoss74–76','The ItemEffects wrapper returns a non-nil handler result unchanged, or false by default for nil. OnStatLoss dispatch uses that wrapper and the actual OnStatLoss map.'),
 ('RC-ITEMEFFECTS','EJECTPACK447–471','EjectPack returns false before consumption for SkyDrop states, opposing side all fainted, wild receiver, inability to switch out, or no legal nonactive member. Normal W26 passes all these separate guards.'),
 ('RC-ITEMEFFECTS','EJECTPACK455–468','After animation/message EjectPack consumes the item before either endOfRound branch or owner-choice request; a negative owner-choice result returns false after that irreversible local prefix and before RecallAndReplace.'),
 ('RC-BATTLERITEM','Remove226–231/Consume233–243','ConsumeItem(true,false) records recycle/Pickup state, conditionally marks belch only for berries, then removes current/initial item as applicable; symbiosis is skipped. Item setter also writes the linked party Pokemon held item.'),
 ('RC-ITEMEFFECTS','EJECTPACK463–469','A nonnegative entry replacement uses ordinary recall/replace, then clears actual old choice, conditionally clears moldBreaker for matching move_user, invokes replacement entry and returns true. W26 excludes a second exit or terminal in that nested entry.'),
 ('RC-ITEMEFFECTS','EJECTPACK458–462','At endOfRound the same consumed-item prefix is followed only by recall-if-alive and OnSwitchOut then true; this handler does not immediately ask for or initialize a replacement.'),
 ('RC-COMMAND','ClearChoice5–11/Command174–196/Loop198–265','At initial entry, clearing a slot choice precedes the first command setup/selection. With the fixture healthy normally selectable replacement, it can choose an action in that first phase; the mid-round no-action effect is not a permanent ban.'),
 ('B17-BATTLE','constructor98–174','Fresh normal Battle construction sets backdrop empty string, backdropBase nil, time0 and environment None before world preparation. These constructor values do not alone describe the eventual recording snapshot.'),
 ('S14','Organized40–67/prepare209–304','The organized wrapper sets internalBattle false then calls world prepare before animation/start; recording properties are taken only once recording start is reached. A prepare exception has no local guarantee of later capture or restoration.'),
 ('S14','prepare270–282','Backdrop priority is non-nil explicit rule, then truthy nextBattleBack, surfing water, nonempty map background, then indoor1 for falsey result. No provided source means indoor1; an explicit empty string is truthy and remains empty rather than taking the fallback.'),
 ('RC-MAPMETA','whole138/constructor92–118','MapMetadata stores battle_background/environment from the supplied hash and exposes readers; it does not synthesize a backdrop or change Cave to the explicit battle-rule environment.'),
 ('S14','prepare264–290','Explicit non-nil environment wins over pbGetEnvironment. Base uses non-nil explicit rule, otherwise Environment.try_get(chosen environment).battle_base; it writes backdropBase only when that base is truthy.'),
 ('RC-ENVIRONMENT','whole131','The complete default Environment registry supplies Grass/TallGrass/ForestGrass base grass, MovingWater/StillWater base water, Puddle base puddle, Sand base sand and Ice base ice; other default entries have nil base. It is independent of MapMetadata environment.'),
 ('S14','prepare291–304','MapMetadata environment Cave unconditionally sets battle.time2 before considering TIME_SHADING, even when chosen battle environment is explicit E. Otherwise time shading reads one time and maps night2/evening1/other0; disabled shading leaves prior time unchanged.'),
 ('RC-TIME','Time4–6/Night50–53/Evening68–71+Settings72','Default TIME_SHADING is true. pbGetTimeNow returns Time.now; Night tests hour>=20 or<5 and Evening tests17<=hour<20. These are static branch contracts, not a host-clock or native-time execution guarantee.'),
 ('R05','Recording47–68/Playback164–180','Recording includes current backdrop/backdropBase/time/environment among the same18 keys; playback writes those recorded fields directly before normal battle start and does not call world prepare to substitute live map/background/time.'),
 ('R10','debug40–49','Debug CTRL skip returns before battle construction/prepare/start/capture. Its messages happen before clearing last_battle_record; no assertion here changes that observed prefix into a clear-before-message sequence.')]
